{"reference":"Psalms 127","book":"Psalms","chapter":127,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Surrounding Psalms","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The psalms surrounding this chapter belong to a group oriented toward worship. Elsewhere in Psalms, communal songs preserve memories of sanctuary destruction and Babylonian exile, while this later group also includes thanksgiving for return, festival praise, and meditation on Torah.","verse_refs":["Psalms 120:1-7","Psalms 121:1-8","Psalms 122:1-9","Psalms 123:1-4","Psalms 124:1-8","Psalms 125:1-5","Psalms 126:1-6","Psalms 128:1-6","Psalms 129:1-8","Psalms 130:1-8","Psalms 131:1-3","Psalms 132:1-18","Psalms 133:1-3","Psalms 134:1-3"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_127_41b3ed5d2e88526c19ee4573"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}